WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.869
-House Democrats unveiled
articles of impeachment

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:05.071
against President Trump.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.106
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.541
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.144 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.880
In the run-up to today's
historic announcement,

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.415
you've heard Trump and his
Republican allies cycle through

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:18.985
one obviously bad faith excuse
after another.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.254
They complained about
the private process,

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.322
then they complained
about the public process.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:26.526
They accused Ukraine of meddling
in the 2016 election.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.862
They said the president was
just worried about corruption

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:31.130
in Ukraine in general.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.600
They said there was
no quid pro quo at all.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.967
During the first
impeachment vote,

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:37.169
they even accused the Democrats
of acting like Soviets

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:39.271
with a very stupid poster.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:40.806
I mean,
look at how dumb this is.

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:43.676
It looks like the cover
of an off-brand board game.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.810
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.879
It's like asking
your grandparents for Risk,

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:50.082
and they show up with something
called "Chance."

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:52.819
[ Gruff voice ] It's fine.
It's the same game.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.021
All those arguments, of course,
are lies.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.157
In reality,
Republicans have no answer

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.424
for one very simple question

00:00:58.424 --> 00:00:59.992
at the heart
of this impeachment process --

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:03.195
Is it okay for the president
to pressure a foreign government

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:04.697
to help him cheat
in an election?

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.500
And my favorite example of this
came last week

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.502
when Republican congressman
Doug Collins,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.271
the ranking member
on the Judiciary Committee

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:13.739
was asked that question
and offered up

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:16.008
some incoherent word puke.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.276
-You keep saying
that the president

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.011
was concerned about corruption,

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:22.081
but in neither of those phone
calls did he mention the word,

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.349
"corruption."

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.951
Why didn't the president mention
the word corruption

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:27.987
and instead ask
the Ukrainian president

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.288
to investigate the Bidens?

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:30.924
-Well, that's almost like
saying, why don't you ask --

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.759
you know, frame your questions
differently?

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.493
He said this is what he wanted
looked into.

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:36.929
He said, can you,
he said, help us as a country

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.197
because we're trying to heal.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.466
We've had --
as Mr. Jordan said earlier,

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.535
and did a great job at it,
we had just come off

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.804
the Mueller hearing, which
was -- most all of you covered

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:48.141
and found to be a total disaster
for the impeachment narrative

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.742
that Democrats have been saying.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.510
What we're simply saying
here is,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.080
is that the issue was
what happened on that call,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.282
and then it became all these
stories from the whistleblowers

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.950
about all these things
that supposedly happened.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.553
And since then, fact witnesses
and even hearsay evidence

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.222
has said, no,
that's not what happened.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:05.992
-Uh, what? Was any --
Was any of that English?

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.627
If you put those words
into Google Translate,

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:10.396
it would just give up.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.831
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:15.068
But that right there...
[ Applause ]

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.837
...is a perfect distillation

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.706
of where the Republicans
are right now.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:22.141
They don't have a coherent
defense, so they just throw out

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:25.178
a string of random buzzwords
as quickly as they can

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.346
and hope people buy it.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.381
In fact, here's GOP congressman
Jim Jordan

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.282
at yesterday's
House Judiciary hearing

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:31.751
basically doing
the same thing --

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.820
just speeding through a bunch
of nonsense as fast as he can.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.856
-Ambassador Taylor recalls
that Mr. Morrison

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.524
told Ambassador Taylor
that I told Mr. Morrison

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.259
that I conveyed this message
to Mr. Yermak

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.161
on September 1, 2019,
in connection with

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.796
Vice President Pence's
visit to Warsaw.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.097
-Oh, my God, man!

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:47.467
Are you reading the evidence
or auctioning it off?

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:50.436
I mean, listen to him.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.572
He sounds like he should
be talking to squirrels

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.140
on a bench in Times Square.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.409
Now, Taylor said to Morrison
that Yermak told Pence

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.077
about his visit to Warsaw.
I mean, isn't that right?

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.845
A pity the pigeon isn't
listening, but the squirrel is.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.113
Oh, wait, he's not.
He's eating a nut.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.949
But where'd he get it?
I don't see a nut tree.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.784
How come we been here
for nine months?!

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:08.021
We don't know where this
squirrel got his nut!

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.722
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.158
Now, compare that to
the measured, judicious tone

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.760
of the Democrats
at the hearing yesterday

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.394
who presented a lengthy
body of evidence

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:17.930
and witness testimony
placing Trump at the center

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.533
of a vast scheme to dangle
hundreds of millions

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:23.235
in taxpayer dollars to Ukraine
in order to get them

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.871
to interfere in the 2020
election on his behalf.

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:30.176
-President Trump's persistent
and continuing effort to coerce

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:34.280
a foreign country to help him
cheat to win an election

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:38.551
is a clear and present danger
to our free and fair elections

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.519
and to our national security.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.655
So, as it relates
to President Trump,

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:47.293
is he an incidental player or
a central player in this scheme?

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.062
-President Trump is the central
player in this scheme.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.130
-And of course he is.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.598
First of all,
we have all the evidence.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.034
Second, I can't imagine Trump
is anything but central.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.268
It's not like he's gonna be

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.036
a supporting player
for someone else.

00:03:58.036 --> 00:04:01.174
He could never be the getaway
driver in a bank robbery.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.242
He'd walk in mid-heist
and be like...

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.977
[ As Trump ] I heard
this is where the action is.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:08.648
Also, you guys,
I think I just got towed.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.216
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.783
[ Normal voice ]
And I think a key moment

00:04:11.783 --> 00:04:14.220
hitting that point home
came in yesterday's hearing

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.221
when Democratic congressman
Eric Swalwell

00:04:16.221 --> 00:04:17.956
and the Democratic Counsel
Daniel Goldman

00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:19.158
laid out all the evidence

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.160
placing Trump at the center
of this scheme.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.530
-Who sent Rudy Giuliani to
Ukraine to smear Joe Biden?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.432
-President Trump.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.834
-Who fired
the anti-corruption ambassador

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.903
in Ukraine, Marie Yavanovitch?

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.371
-President Trump.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:35.475
-Who told Ambassador Sondland
and Ambassador Volker

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:39.245
to Ru-- to work with
Rudy Giuliani on Ukraine?

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.546
-President Trump.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.783
-Who ordered his own
Chief of Staff, Mick Mulvaney,

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:47.019
to withhold critical military
assistance for Ukraine?

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.254
-President Trump.

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:51.523
-Who refused to meet
with President Zelensky

00:04:51.523 --> 00:04:53.893
in the Oval Office?
-President Trump.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.128
-Who asked President Zelensky
for a favor?

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:58.397
-President Trump.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.232
-Who personally asked
President Zelensky

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:03.669
to investigate
his political rival, Joe Biden?

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:04.937
-President Trump.
-Oh, my God,

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.739
the answer to every question
was President Trump.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.040
I want to do one!

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.142
Who stands like he's playing
the Leaning Tower of Pisa

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:12.178
in a school play?

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.713
President Trump.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:16.516
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:19.285
The Democrats diligently laid
out every piece of evidence

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.687
linking Trump to this scheme,

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:22.221
and Republicans
rebutted none of it.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.722
The facts here are actually
very simple --

00:05:23.722 --> 00:05:24.991
Yes, there was a quid pro quo,

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.658
and yes, it was to investigate
the Bidens.

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:29.095
And the basic truth is
Republicans in the White House

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.263
just don't care.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.098
They want us all to just
accept it and move on.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.932
They've already said as much.

00:05:33.932 --> 00:05:36.402
-Was there a quid pro quo?

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:39.004
-As I testified previously,

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:41.607
with regard to the requested
White House call

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.710
and the White House meeting,
the answer is yes.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.680
-What exactly did you
hope Zelensky would do

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.715
about the Bidens
after your phone call?

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:53.752
-Well, I would think that
if they were honest about it,

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:56.856
they'd start a major
investigation into the Bidens.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.358
-Let's be clear. What you just
described is a quid pro quo.

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:02.661
-We do that all the time
with foreign policy.

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.763
And I have news for everybody --
Get over it.

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:05.764
-Get over it?

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:07.667
These guys are such ass[bleep]

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.436
they talk like dumb truck stop
bumper stickers.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.471
"My other ride is your mom.
Get over it."

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:15.307
[ Laughter ]
But that's their real argument.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.476
You can pretty much ignore
everything else they say --

00:06:17.476 --> 00:06:20.112
All the process complaints,
the buzzwords, the brain vomit.

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:21.380
The Republicans' argument
is simple --

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.815
We can do whatever we want.
Get over it.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.217
Well, today,
House Democrats responded

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.551
by telling the Trump White House

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.719
that they will definitely not
just get over it.

00:06:27.719 --> 00:06:29.188
-An historic day
on Capitol Hill.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.323
The House announcing articles
of impeachment

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:33.860
against the sitting
U.S. president, Donald Trump,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.061
two articles specifically --

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.196
abuse of power
and obstruction of Congress.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:40.966
-Today, in service to our duty
to the Constitution

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:44.871
and to our country, the House
Committee on the Judiciary

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:47.373
is introducing
two articles of impeachment

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:50.042
charging the President
of the United States,

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:55.047
Donald J. Trump, with committing
high crimes and misdemeanors.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.316
-That's right.
Today, Democrats unveiled

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.518
two articles of impeachment
against President Trump,

00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:01.153
but if you ask me,
he got off easy.

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:02.521
Remember, the guy also

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:04.256
obstructed justice
in the Mueller probe,

00:07:04.256 --> 00:07:06.492
violated the Constitution
by enriching himself,

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:08.661
inflicted human rights abuses
on migrant children,

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:11.029
and directed an illegal scheme
to pay hush money

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:12.298
to cover up an affair.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:15.067
It's not even hard to find
the crimes with this guy.

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:16.402
It's like a Where's Waldo?

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:19.038
where Waldo is
right in the middle of the map

00:07:19.038 --> 00:07:21.607
with a giant bag of cash
in one hand

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.909
and giving you the finger
with the other one.

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:26.645
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:28.714
As Democrats argued
in the press conference today,

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:31.350
you can't wait until an election
to remove a president

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.852
who's made clear he's willing
to cheat in that election.

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:36.288
In fact, today,
as Democrats were unveiling

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:38.224
articles of impeachment,
Trump was welcoming

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:40.526
the Russian Foreign Minister
Sergey Lavrov

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:43.162
into the White House,
and a White House spokesman

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:44.930
actually said on Fox News
this morning

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.566
that the two would discuss
election security.

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:50.235
-President Trump meets Russia's
Foreign Secretary Lavrov

00:07:50.235 --> 00:07:52.271
at the White House
this afternoon.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:55.507
Now, we're told that this
is about arms control.

00:07:55.507 --> 00:07:57.142
But it's gonna look real bad.

00:07:57.142 --> 00:08:00.078
It's gonna be Russia,
Russia, Russia, Sergey Lavrov.

00:08:00.078 --> 00:08:02.782
It's gonna get bad PR out of it,
isn't it?

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.083
-I don't think so.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.618
Listen, these kind of
conversations are critical.

00:08:06.618 --> 00:08:08.787
You know, it's incumbent upon
any American president

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:10.989
to try and build relationships
across the globe.

00:08:10.989 --> 00:08:13.359
We're absolutely expected
to talk about arms control,

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:15.260
but also election security.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.130
-He's gonna discuss election
security with the Russians?

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.999
That's like airing
a "Say No To Drugs" PSA

00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:23.502
with Walter White.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:26.272
At this point, all Trump and his
allies have left is one thing --

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:27.706
lying about the investigations

00:08:27.706 --> 00:08:28.874
and claiming
there's some sort of

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:31.243
treasonous deep-state witch hunt
to overthrow him.

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:32.477
Yesterday, for example,

00:08:32.477 --> 00:08:34.847
a Justice Department
Inspector General's report

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:37.049
found that while there
were serious errors

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:38.651
in the FBI's Russia
investigation,

00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:41.820
there was no anti-Trump plot
and the investigation was both

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.255
unbiased and justified.

00:08:43.255 --> 00:08:45.591
The report debunked
Trump's conspiracy theory

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:47.493
that he was spied on
or that it was an attempt

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:49.361
by the Obama administration
to overthrow him.

00:08:49.361 --> 00:08:52.698
And yet, today, Trump lashed out
at his own FBI Director,

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:55.301
Christopher Wray,
for agreeing with that report.

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:57.269
-Breaking news --
A long-awaited report

00:08:57.269 --> 00:08:59.404
from the Justice Department's
Inspector General

00:08:59.404 --> 00:09:01.774
finding the FBI's launch
of the Russia probe

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:04.743
was valid and unbiased.

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:07.112
The report also says
that there was no spying

00:09:07.112 --> 00:09:09.448
on the Trump campaign,
which is a conspiracy theory

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:12.084
that Trump has pushed
since taking office.

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:14.119
-It's important
that the Inspector General

00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:16.856
found that
in this particular instance,

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:19.791
the investigation was opened

00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:23.162
with appropriate predication
and authorization.

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:27.499
-Just minutes after that aired,
President Trump tweeted this --

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:30.736
"I don't know what report
current Director of the FBI

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:32.304
Christopher Wray was reading,

00:09:32.304 --> 00:09:34.339
but it sure wasn't the one
given to me.

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:36.975
-Oh, it wasn't?
Well, maybe the report you got

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:38.410
didn't match the actual report

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.347
since the actual report
was 434 pages long.

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:44.684
Trump's aides probably gave him
a one-page memo that read,

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:46.985
"You were right again, boss!"
[ Laughter ]

00:09:46.985 --> 00:09:49.855
But there's another argument
on top of all the lying

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:51.857
and conspiracy theories
that infuriating.

00:09:51.857 --> 00:09:54.026
Trump and the GOP have also
argued that impeachment

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:56.362
is somehow hurting the country
and preventing the government

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:59.297
from helping people, even while
the Trump White House itself

00:09:59.297 --> 00:10:01.400
is actively hurting
the most vulnerable.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.501
-As you head into Christmas

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:04.403
and you head into
the holiday season,

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:07.305
people are gonna want results
from Congress, and right now,

00:10:07.305 --> 00:10:09.074
all they're getting
is hatred, vitriol,

00:10:09.074 --> 00:10:11.777
and a sham impeachment hearing
that doesn't do anything

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:15.247
to put food on the tables
of the American people.

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:18.083
-Oh, now you're worried about
putting food on people's tables?

00:10:18.083 --> 00:10:21.153
Last week, you guys kicked
700,000 people off food stamps

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:23.322
by imposing awful
new work requirements.

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:24.890
Think about how cruel that is.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.292
Work requirements from a guy
who never works.

00:10:27.292 --> 00:10:29.861
Trump spends most of his time
tweeting, watching TV,

00:10:29.861 --> 00:10:32.131
and crawling around his
golf course like a groundhog

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:34.366
who just popped
out of the 18th hole,

00:10:34.366 --> 00:10:37.136
looks like he's auditioning
for the role of the gopher

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:40.439
in a remake of "Caddyshack."

00:10:40.439 --> 00:10:43.141
That --
That's the kind of cruelty

00:10:43.141 --> 00:10:45.444
Republicans have committed
themselves to defending,

00:10:45.444 --> 00:10:46.979
and they're fine with doing it.

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:49.281
Today, Democrats at least
put down a marker

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:50.783
and said there will be
consequences

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:53.052
for Trump's behavior.
They asked a simple question --

00:10:53.052 --> 00:10:55.654
Should a president be allowed
to cheat to win an election?

00:10:55.654 --> 00:10:57.590
And instead of offering
a coherent defense,

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.124
all Republicans could say was...

00:10:59.124 --> 00:11:00.459
-Why don't you ask -- you know,

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:02.060
frame your questions
differently?

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:03.729
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:05.130
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:07.233 line:0%
♪♪

